## Earlier themes

**Moomin fun.** The very first Moomintroll comics, published in Ny Tid. Translations into English
and commentary in [Moomintroll and the End of the World: Tove Jansson's first Moomin comic strip with essays on her life and work](http://www.adlibris.com/fi/product.aspx?isbn=9519667598),
edited by Trygve Söderling and Anna Rotkirch (Helsingfors: Tigertext, 2008).

**Russian family and gender studies.** With my St Petersburg colleagues Anna Temkina, Elena
Zdravomyslova and others I have studied Russian gender relations, with publications on the
commercialisation of everyday life, paid domestic workers in Russia, the practices and values of
Russian sexual therapists, and the reception of the maternity capital programme.

**Experiences of oocyte donors.** Our survey of oocyte donors in Finland resulted in two articles
in *Human Reproduction*:
[Short- and long-term health consequences and current satisfaction levels for altruistic anonymous, identity-release and known oocyte donors](https://academic.oup.com/humrep/article/31/3/597/2384626)
and [Attitudes of anonymous and identity-release oocyte donors towards future contact with donor offspring](https://academic.oup.com/humrep/article-abstract/34/4/672/5364894).

**Friendship.** The [Friendship Fraternity Study](http://www.theffs.nl/) followed young people's
close friendship groups.

**Feminist history of ideas.** Essays on the life and loves of Alexandra Kollontay were published
in Finnish in [Naisia Venäjän kulttuurihistoriassa](http://www.gaudeamus.fi/naisia-venajan/), in
Swedish in a [Scandinavian anthology](https://ibok.no/bok/9788274772878), and as a
[Kollontay–Colette comparison](https://blogs.helsinki.fi/rotkirch/files/2018/12/kollontay-and-colette.pdf).
